<article class="env-proposition" id="0D04">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0D04">Proposition <span data-tag="0D04">99.10.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to B$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. If $f$ is flat, of finite presentation, and proper, then $\mathcal{P}\! \mathit{ic}_{X/B}$ is an algebraic stack. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate consequence of Lemma <a href="/tag/0D03" data-tag="0D03">99.10.1</a>, Algebraic Stacks, Lemma <a href="/tag/05UM" data-tag="05UM">94.15.4</a> and either Theorem <a href="/tag/08WC" data-tag="08WC">99.5.12</a> or Theorem <a href="/tag/09DS" data-tag="09DS">99.6.1</a> 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>